1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,240
My wife's pulse is a steady seventy beats per minute, which proves she is lying to me right now.

2
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:15,756
For ten years, my job as a forensic polygraph expert taught me that humans always betray themselves through tiny tremors.

3
00:00:16,056 --> 00:00:22,704
Elena smiled at me across the kitchen island, pouring morning coffee with hands that never shook once.

4
00:00:23,004 --> 00:00:31,692
Normal humans sweat. Their pupils dilate. Their vocal pitch rises when they fabricate even the smallest details.

5
00:00:31,992 --> 00:00:39,384
Yet Elena's vitals remained impossibly calm when she swore she never left the house yesterday afternoon.

6
00:00:39,684 --> 00:00:46,332
I checked the security logs on her smart implant, searching for the glitch that kept her heart rate so flat.

7
00:00:46,632 --> 00:00:54,528
The screen didn't show a glitch. It displayed a fatal car crash report dated three full years ago.

8
00:00:54,828 --> 00:01:02,388
I spun around in terror as the woman I loved stood silently in the doorway, casting no shadow.

9
00:01:02,688 --> 00:01:09,624
She stepped closer, her synthetic eyes glowing faintly in the dark, whispering that she was built just for me.

10
00:01:09,924 --> 00:01:15,108
If she isn't real, why did her heartbeat just match my own terrified rhythm?
